SIMPLE QUERY INSERT SELECT DATA FILTER in mongo db



1. Insert Data: To insert data into a MongoDB collection, use the insertOne() or insertMany() methods.

    -------------------------------------

    // Insert a single document
    db.collectionName.insertOne({ key1: "value1", key2: "value2" });

    example:
    db.employee.insertOne({DrName:"Dr. Kamal sharma",Specilization:"cordilogy",designation:"sr.doctor",degree:"MBBS,MD"})
    ***********************************
    // Insert multiple documents
    db.collectionName.insertMany([
    { key1: "value1a", key2: "value2a" },
    { key1: "value1b", key2: "value2b" }
    ]);

    example:

    db.employee.insertMany([{DrName:"Dr. Prabha salve",Specilization:"cordilogy",designation:"jr. doctor",degree:"MBBS"},{DrName:"Dr. Rahul Gupta",Specilization:"Dentist",desicnation:"jr. Doctor",degree:"MBBS"})

    -------------------------------------

2. Select Data: To query (select) data, use the find() method.

    -------------------------------------

    // Select all documents
    db.collectionName.find({});

    // Select documents with a filter
    db.collectionName.find({ key1: "value1" });
    
    example:

    db.employee.find({degree:"MBBS"})
    -------------------------------------

3. Data Filtering: You can filter documents using various conditions in the find() method.

    -------------------------------------
    
    // Select documents where key1 equals "value1"
    db.collectionName.find({ key1: "value1" });

    // Select documents where key2 is greater than a value
    db.collectionName.find({ key2: { $gt: 10 } });

    // Select documents with multiple conditions
    db.collectionName.find({ key1: "value1", key2: { $lte: 20 } });

    -------------------------------------

4.Update in MongoDB
    You can use updateOne, updateMany, or replaceOne methods to update documents in a collection.

    1. updateOne()
    This method updates a single document that matches the filter.

    Syntex
    ------------------------------------
    db.collection.updateOne(filter, update, options)
    ------------------------------------

    Example

    -----------------------------------
    db.users.updateOne(
        { username: "john_doe" },  // Filter
        { $set: { age: 30 } }      // Update
    );
    -----------------------------------
    2. updateMany()
    This method updates multiple documents that match the filter.
-
    Syntax:
    -----------------------------------
    db.collection.updateMany(filter, update, options)
    -----------------------------------
    Example
    ----------------------------------
    db.users.updateMany(
        { isActive: false },         // Filter
        { $set: { status: "inactive" } } // Update
    );
    ----------------------------------

    3. replaceOne()
    This method replaces an entire document that matches the filter.

    Syntax:
    ------------------------------------
    db.collection.replaceOne(filter, replacement, options)
    ------------------------------------

    Example
    ------------------------------------
    db.users.replaceOne(
        { username: "john_doe" }, 
        { username: "john_doe", age: 30, status: "active" } // New document
    );
    ------------------------------------

5. Delete in MongoDB

    You can use deleteOne or deleteMany methods to remove documents from a collection.

    1. deleteOne()
    This method deletes a single document that matches the filter.

    Syntax:

    --------------------------------------
    db.collection.deleteOne(filter)
    --------------------------------------

    Examples
    --------------------------------------
    db.users.deleteOne({ username: "john_doe" });
    --------------------------------------

    2. deleteMany()
    This method deletes multiple documents that match the filter.

    Syntax:
    ----------------------------------------
    db.collection.deleteMany(filter)
    ----------------------------------------

    Example
    ----------------------------------------
    db.users.deleteMany({ isActive: false });
    ----------------------------------------
